# PLAN CLI LAUNCH — 12 agents for real --exec

File: openOODA/audit/plan_cli_launch.oot
Ship 2. Today cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo on --exec runs:
  sh -c "test -e <path>; exit 0"
That checks that the file exists. It does not run the payload.
pm_launch_gate already checks yank, sha256, and cap subset.

## 0. Done when

  1. After gate returns ok, --exec runs the pinned `.oo` with the
     same path as `ooda run <payload>` (run_oodac_run / host_run).
  2. Without --exec, print the path only. Do not run.
  3. Gate fail: non-zero exit. No payload process. No
     `ooda launch: ok`.
  4. Yank after install, sha drift, and extra caps still refuse
     with --exec (qa/pm_hostile_spine.oo).
  5. A new fixture with `pub fn main` prints LAUNCH_EXEC_OK
     when launched with --exec.
  6. Public registry hello.oo has no main. Do not change it.
     Do not treat hello_ok as a program.
  7. Do not grow ooda/pm/. Product is cli/.

## 1. Waves

  Wave 0 (read): COORD, RT, DOCS, SEC
  Wave 1 (write): DE1, DE2, HARN
  Wave 2 (lock): HYG
  Wave 3 (attack): PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM
  Wave 4 (prove): INT
  Wave 5: COORD

## 2. Twelve agents

  COORD
    Worktree branch `wip/launch-exec`.
    File lock: cmd_pm_launch.oo, optional pm_launch.oo,
    new fixture dir, new smoke, qa/pm_hostile_spine.oo.
    Do not edit main.oo.

  DE1
    Own cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo.
    Delete the `test -e` shell line.
    If gate is not ok: same die path as today.
    If --exec and gate ok: call run_oodac_run on the payload path.
    Propagate the child exit code.
    If --json and --exec: do not claim ok before the run finishes.

  DE2
    Own cli/pm_launch.oo only if the gate string API must change.
    Prefer no edit. If DE1 can call the existing `ok` / `err …`
    strings, DE2 writes a read-only note and stops.
    If a change is required, keep yank / sha / caps order.

  RT
    Read only. Exec must use existing SysCap host_run, not a new
    C spawn API. If run_oodac_run cannot take a CAS path, name
    the blocker. Do not patch chs_rt.

  HARN
    New fixtures/pm_launch_exec/: manifest + payload with
    `pub fn main` that prints LAUNCH_EXEC_OK.
    New scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo:
      add from that vendor, launch without --exec (path only,
      no LAUNCH_EXEC_OK), launch with --exec (sees LAUNCH_EXEC_OK).
    Extend qa/pm_hostile_spine.oo: --exec on yank / tamper / extra
    caps still refuse and must not print LAUNCH_EXEC_OK.

  PV1
    Attack: --exec on a missing lock name, a name with `..`,
    a yanked name, a drifted CAS file.
    Each must fail closed. No child `oodac run`.

  PV2
    Attack: payload that is not `.oo` (ELF / empty / directory).
    Refuse. Do not `sh` the bytes.
    Attack: --exec without a prior add.

  SEC
    No `sh -c` around the payload. Quote rules stay in host_run.
    Caps: launch grant must still be a subset of the lock need.
    OODA_FS_WRITEDIR must not widen because we exec.
    SECRET: do not print CAS bytes.

  MEM
    One child per --exec. Child must be reaped (no zombie).
    Hang budget 10 seconds on the smoke payload.
    Do not leave .ooda-cache junk outside the smoke dir.

  INT
    Rebuild CLI with seed oodac.
    Run pm_launch_exec_smoke twice.
    Run the hostile spine twice (double-run on refuse cases).
    Confirm oodac/oodac binary timestamp is unchanged.

  HYG
    Line counts on cmd_pm_launch.oo (121 today; room exists).
    Academy headers on new files. No leftover vendor lock in
    the worktree after smokes.

  DOCS
    No site edits. Audit note: `--exec` means run, not exists.
    Help text in cmd_pm_launch header must match the code.

## 3. Failure

  If DE1 cannot call run_oodac_run without editing host_run.oo,
  COORD stops and asks the parent. host_run.oo is shared.
  Do not silently edit it.
